06/08/2025 13:05:10 - Kiu Hong Adrian Wong (Work notes)
Queried this with Account Director - Simon Maskell

Good afternoon Simon, 

I hope you’re well? 

I’m reaching out from Acute Meds Man Support regarding NGH’s ticket CS1610842. 

They are wanting to test a new PAS feed (used to SEND messages into our Meds Man system). To do this, they are adjusting the message format manually, to have our system accept it – However they are experiencing issues. 

Would it be advisable for them to raise a project for this? I’m aware that NLAG did something similar, where the PAS feed was changed without a project and it’s caused issues down the line – to this day in fact. 

Kind Regards,

Adrian Wong

05/08/2025 14:25:51 - Kiu Hong Adrian Wong (Work notes)
Meeting: 

Advised of reasons why this should be a project:

1. If a new message format is being sent - we may need to configure our interface to accept the messages/ acks sent back.
2. New messages may require varying levels of processing power - this needs to be tested - to ensure message processing is not impacted for years down the line.
3. Changes to message format needs to be documented on a schema, for effective future support.
4. If a project is set up for this, you will have dedicated resource to test and resolve issues that may arise.

Basically want to avoid what happened to NLAG - didn't mention NLAG specifically. 

------------------------------
