30/07/2025 12:04:21 - Kiu Hong Adrian Wong (Work notes)
/*ePMA systems when a prescriber selects penicillamine as an allergy in error instead of penicillin due to penicillamine coming up first in the alphabet. This is an issue on Optum ePMA at NLaG.

We can’t see who has been marked as being allergic to penicillamine, as it is not a reportable field so any reports need to come off the live database. We may need help with that.

I am aware that unlike our partners on the north bank, Optum ePMA does give a warning if penicillin is prescribed to a patient marked as allergic to penicillamine. Unfortunately, as we are now governed by the north bank, and they use an inferior product, they have had multiple occasions of this. However, they can run reports to show all the data. Therefore, they are pressuring us to prove that. We think that we are ok now, but we don’t know when that interaction was added to the system, so we may have patients marked as allergic to penicillamine and not penicillin from 2013



'As it is not a reportable field so any reports need to come off the live database. We may need help with that.'

Script below displays all patients that have had the allergy 'Penicillamine, including the date of when the allergy was recorded. 
Earliest allergy entry against Penicillamine is '2013-08-06 11:34:44.000'
56 rows returned, however - many are TEST patients.
*/
-----
SELECT DISTINCT
    p.Description as 'Allergy',
    a.CreatedDate as 'Allergy recorded date',
	ea.alias as 'Patient HospID',
	e.Description as 'Episode',
	e.EndDate as 'Episode Ended'
FROM DssAllergy A
JOIN Product P ON A.ProductID = P.ProductID
JOIN episode e on a.EpisodeID = e.episodeid
JOIN EntityAlias ea on e.EntityID = ea.EntityID
WHERE P.ProductID IN (
    SELECT ProductID 
    FROM Product
    WHERE Description LIKE '%penicillamine%'
)
and ea.AliasGroupID = 22
ORDER BY A.CreatedDate;

/*
'But we don’t know when that interaction was added to the system, so we may have patients marked as allergic to penicillamine and not penicillin from 2013'

The below script displays when alerts have been overriden againsted Penicillamine allergy - including the requested drug that triggered the allergy alert. 
We can see, the earliest override was for a drug requested on 2013-09-17 16:14:44.000.
15 rows returned - meaning 26 times a patient had a recorded allergy of Penicillamine and had the allergy warning overriden. However, none of the requested drugs are Penicillin - from what I can see, apart from the TEST I did on 2025-07-28 11:30:00.000. 
*/
SELECT DISTINCT
    r.description AS 'Requested Drug',
    wo.Description AS 'WarningOverride',
	r.CreatedDate as 'request creation',
	ea.alias as 'Patient'
FROM DssWarningOverride WO
JOIN DSSALERTTYPE AT ON wo.AlertType = at.DSSAlertTypeID
JOIN EpisodeOrderLinkDssWarningOverride ELWO ON wo.DssWarningOverrideID = elwo.DssWarningOverrideID
JOIN request r ON elwo.RequestID = r.Requestid
JOIN episodeorder eo on r.RequestID = eo.RequestID
JOIN episode e on eo.EpisodeID = e.EpisodeID
JOIN EntityAlias ea on e.EntityID = ea.EntityID
WHERE wo.Description LIKE '%penicillamine%'
  AND at.DSSAlertTypeID = 1
  AND ea.AliasGroupID = 22
  order by r.CreatedDate
/*

Conclusion - The behaviour of Optum where'ePMA does give a warning if penicillin is prescribed to a patient marked as allergic to penicillamine.'appears to have been in place since 2013. 
This link was introduced in 2013 at the latest - involving the table 'ChemicalGroupRelation'.

