Need to go back a few steps - Does the PRB even match?

You've linked the case to PRB0050103 - although the description does seem to match, need to supply evidence for this. (Although, from the screenshots that the customer attached - I can't see the 'Linked Prescription' icon - however, was this unlinked since?)

To understand if PRB0050103  matches the case, you need to check whether the customer's example matches the description of the PRB. 

To match with PRB0050103 , the prescription must have been linked whilst the supply request was raised, then discontinued or amended whilst the supply request was pending. (see the Pharmacy Dispensing user guide and CTRL+F 'Linked')

I.e.
1. Check that patient 50937994's Zuclopenthixol tab 20mg was a linked prescription. 
2. If it doesn't appear to be a linked prescription - was it previously? Check the History, was it linked, then unlinked? - note down the dates/times
3. If it was linked, was the prescription, or the one(s) it was linked with - discontinued or amended - whilst the supply request was pending? 

If the answer is 'Yes' to number 3, then the PRB matches. 

(If you've already gone though this process, please ensure its documented as work notes)

