I have linked this to PRB0051371

Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem -

Case relogged from CS1151166 which was linked to PRB0051371 which was relogged from CS1137742

""
CS1137742 - L2 Case was with Michael

Advice given was 

I've checked this with Product and the Contract Uploader will add new contracts not amend existing ones. If the current contract is being terminated early you would need to go onto the Pharmacy Product Editor and remove the old contract, then add the new one on with the correct dates via the Contract Uploader.
""
---
""
CS1151166 - L2 case was with Adrian

Advise given was

When amending the stop date, this is proposing a new contract. This means the original contract (with the original end date) will still be present on the database. So when the End Date of the new proposed contact is met, the underlying contract with the original end date will take over again.

Instead of editing the supplier contract, please complete the following:

1. Access the 'Edit Supplier Profile' for the specific product.
2. Add a New Supplier Profile, with the new contract information (that is to replace the original) - make this the primary supplier.
3. Delete the original contract that you wanted to end.

We still have the PRB open, our product team are still reviewing this.

Your individual case has been linked to PRB0051371 and the workaround is state above. Your individual case will now be marked as resolved, but you can track the progress of PRB0051371 and any fixes on Optum Help Centre https://www.optumhelpcentre.co.uk/csm by searching for PRB0051371.

Please note that our Known Error reasons are as follows:

Fix in progress - Awaiting change - Fixes being provided outside of a main release development.

Fix in progress - Awaiting release - A fix has been prioritised and moved into development of the next release.

Fix deferred - PRBs that will not be fixed in BAU releases but will be addressed in our modernisation releases.

Fix not possible - The fix is not viable due to technology dependencies?and a workaround is available.

No fix available - The fix is not viable due to lack of priority status or technology dependencies?and a workaround is available.
""

Trust is now advising this does not work

""
This is now the third case logged for this issue (the last being CS1151166). The contracts have been terminated using the process that Optum provided on CS1151166 - i.e. ending the contract, then deleting the supplier. Even though this process has been followed as suggested , it is only part working. It is still listed as part of the contracts on the contracts tab, but when you go to update the contract as the completed contracted supplier has been deleted as per their advice, it's not coming up as an option for me to try and amend the dates again.  See examples attached.
""

