09/09/2025 10:14:25 - Azeem Parvez (Work notes)
Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem -

The trust is experiencing slowness across all machines are different times intermittently (every few days).

it is very difficult to say if it happens to everyone at the exact same time. It is however, affecting all wards and all community teams, including our pharmacy and so if I need to do a test like that I will. So far the trends I am seeing are;

-If the EPMA login screen is slow to open and display, then logging into the system and using the system itself will then be immensely slow.  

-If the cache, cookies and temporary files of Internet Explorer are deleted on the machine, and the machine is restarted, EPMA returns to a normal fast speed again, however, this does not seem to last and by the next day the machine can become slow again.

-In instances where the slow issue has occurred the customer has connected to a web server, after restarting and EPMA resuming to normal speed, I have been re-connected to the very same web server, except the speed is normal.

-This issue is now becoming a daily occurrence, as well as with a number of staff who are now regularly reporting this issue; often highlighting it as a clinical risk.

--The issue does not occur at specific times

- Anti virus exclusions have also been checked.

-The issue does not seem to be DB or web server related as the system loads and works fine on the web server. Does not also seem to be load balancer related. Seems like an issue on the client side. The only resolution that seems to work is when clearing the cache in the browser settings, however this only seems to be a temp fix and the issue could happen again the same day. 

The 10.23 hap client setup guide has been followed and changes have been put in place to mirror this, however performance remained slow after applying these changes - no difference made. 

See Attached configuration of some clients and logs of what has been happening. 


Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -  

the issues with slowness actually started between April and May 2024 last year, but have steadily got worse and since February this year have been particularly bad.

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -See attached or summary

Look to include screenshots where possible -see attached

Details of the system configuration (region/organisation etc.) - See attached

Details on the user or user type reporting the issue - n/a

Machine specific or full hardware estate impacted e.g. Printing failure for all or one specific user/machine? -all

Details on any relevant data condition (organisation/user/patient/system) -n/a

Clinical Safety / Security / Information Governance Risk -potential clinical risk

Clinical Safety / Information Governance statement -slow system could cause delay in patient treatment when the slowness occurs.

Workaround offered or provided – Clear the cache which is a temporary fix

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - see summary

A clear set of recreation steps -n/a

