20/08/2025 15:17:19 - Michael Carter (Work notes)
This is PRB0049998. This explains it best from case CS0935018:

""
Hi Jonathan,

Just an update on the PRB this case is attached to regarding duplicating returns. We have managed to replicate this on another site. The steps taken to do so are as follows:

1) Go to a Dispensing desktop like ""WGH Aseptics - Dispensing 122""
2) Search for a patient
3) Prescribe a batch manufactured product
4) Dispense the product with batch A
5) Select the line underneath the prescription and press Dispense (this is a re-dispense that overwrites the line written)
6) On the re-dispense issue batch B
7) Again press Dispense on the same line again (The embedded line underneath the prescription)
8) Return batch A with the option of ""Return ingredients and undo manufactured issue""
9) Press Dispense again on the embedded line and this time return batch B with ""Return ingredients and undo manufactured issue"".

On the transaction log at this point the first 3 transactions are correct (Issue A, Issue B, Return A) but on the return of batch B it doubles down and returns it twice.

As this is hard coded we have logged it with development to fix in a later version. The workaround provided for this in current versions is that we can turn off the ability to re-dispense on all the Dispensing desktops. You can still press dispense on the line to return products, but it will not allow you to dispense a new batch to that line instead it gives a pop up to say that ""The allow re-dispense setting is not enabled on this desktop"".

I've changed the setting on your Test environment just on the desktop ""WGH Aseptics - Dispensing 122"" so that you can try the warning pop up. If after giving that a try you want us to raise a change to do the same on Live let us know and we can do that.
""

