Worth noting that with option 2 it will always appear as available on the Medicines Due For Ward under the PRN tab.

13/08/2025 15:45:17 - Michael Carter (Work notes)
Had the meeting with Mark H and Coleen from Clinical. Coleen is updating the CIR to say that we don't think this is patient harm. For my tasks I need to explain to the customer the difference between If Required and When Required. Then as we don't have functionality for If Required anymore give them some work arounds. The work arounds would be:

1) Prescribe this as once a day at 22:00 with some direction text that says only to be given if the patient requires it. This would then appear on the Medicines Due For Ward desktop and the users would need to either mark it as Given or Not Given each day.
2) Option 2 would be to keep it as a When Required but put a note on the Prescription or Direction text to say only to be given at 22:00 and only if the patient requires it.

I need to go onto the test environment and check what displays on the Drug chart that would make the distinction clear that it is only to be given at 22:00.

