20/08/2025 17:19:07 - Swati Dongare (Work notes)
Investigation:

Check the flow of data for the 'Period'

Looking on Report Builder:

What the user chooses:
- Parameters available are set by 'days'
- Formulated by:
'select p.Description, p.Period_Days as days from icwsys.PARPeriod p
where p.Period_days > 0'
- produces an Integer.

However, the main query looks at @Startdate - we know the pPAR_Report_Detail is correct, because when executing the below, the correct restrictions to StartDate is being applied - when setting the startdate manually.

Meaning the issue is upstream. I.e. How @StartDate is generated.
-----------------------
USE [EHSC_HAP_LIVE]
GO

DECLARE @return_value int

EXEC @return_value = [icwsys].[pPAR_Report_Detail]
@EpisodeID = 162488,
@StartDate = N'2025-08-04 13:32:08.247',
@Show_prescriptions_only = 1


SELECT 'Return Value' = @return_value

GO
-----------------------


How is @Startdate generated?
- ReportBuilder > Parameters > StartDate > Properties.

1. General tab > DataType - currently set to 'Integer - this must be wrong, as we can see above, that it should be a datetime.

2. Default Values > Get Values from a query - Currently set to:
Dataset: Days
Value field: Days
This looks wrong too, because we know the @days is an integer, but the @startdate should be a datetime.


-----------------------

FIX:
1. Report Builder > Parameters > StartDate > Properties > General tab > DataType
Change to Date/Time

2. Report Builder > Parameters > StartDate > Properties > Default Values > Get Values from a query
Change to:
Dataset: startDate
Value field: startDate

