23/03/2026 13:21:59 - Ian Holden (Work notes)
Hi Ian,

I would like to follow up on the issue where individual users experience very slow performance when using ePMA, which is usually resolved after a full shutdown, waiting two minutes, and then restarting the device.

This issue has recently gained significant attention following the CQC visit, and there is increasing pressure to identify the root cause and implement a sustainable solution. It is impacting clinical work and is highly inconvenient for users to repeatedly restart their devices.

Any update will be much appreciated.

Many thanks,
Hui

25/02/2026 12:44:17 - Ian Holden (Work notes)
Hi all,

I understand the request from the Optum colleagues to cancel the regular meeting. Given that there has not been a major system outage recently, I am happy for the meeting to be cancelled.

However, I would like Dynatrace monitoring to remain in place. Although the major system outage has not reoccurred, it does appear to happen approximately every six months. The last incident was at the end of August, so based on that pattern, it could potentially happen again between now and early March. My concern is that if Dynatrace is removed and a major outage occurs, we would have to wait for another occurrence to capture the data needed to identify the root cause.

That said, we continue to receive reports from individual users experiencing very slow performance when using ePMA. The issue is usually resolved after a full shutdown, waiting two minutes, and then restarting the device. The explanation we have provided to users is that this clears the cache and reconnects them to a less congested server. Has there been any further update on this? This has been a constant source of frustration for users, and I would really like to see improvements.

Many thanks,
Hui

