12/09/2025 14:41:01 - Ian Holden (Work notes)
Optum Meeting Summary
Incident Overview & Context: The team discussed an intermittent failover issue affecting the Essex partnership's EPMA system, which has occurred twice this week. The failover is used as a workaround, making root cause investigation difficult. The issue impacts drug administration rounds, but is not currently classified as a medium clinical risk due to its frequency.
Monitoring Solution (Dynatrace) Deployment: The main action is to deploy Dynatrace for infrastructure monitoring on the customer's servers, aiming for installation on Monday morning. Each server will require a reboot, but downtime can be staggered using failover. Ian will handle installation with support from Dario's team. 
Technical Details & Next Steps: Dynatrace will provide resource metrics (CPU, memory, etc.) and basic monitoring. Advanced SQL monitoring is possible but requires additional infrastructure and permissions, which may be considered if initial data is insufficient. The team will clarify with the customer about their DBA resources and the possibility of setting up an additional server for deeper monitoring. 
Ownership & Communication: Kamlesh and Heather will coordinate customer communications, ensuring all technical questions are answered. Chris provided firewall and endpoint details for the customer. The team will confirm alert routing for Dynatrace to ensure timely response to incidents.
Previous Actions & Investigation: Past investigations identified a problematic query related to the drug chart, and a patch was previously applied, which temporarily helped. Indexing jobs and server specs have been reviewed and corrected as needed. The team will continue to monitor for recurrence and escalate if the situation worsens. 
Action Items & Follow-up: The team will proceed with Dynatrace installation, monitor resource usage, and adjust alerting as needed. Ian will handle installation with support from Dario's team They will reconvene after initial monitoring data is available or sooner if the issue escalates. 
Next meeting to be Monday after monitoring solution has been implemented.

