26/08/2025 12:58:56 - Swati Dongare (Work notes)
Our EPMA went down this morning (case ref CS1638269) and our SSHIS looked at this, and the issue was related to patching of EPMA SQL.  Last month we had a similar issue where when the automated patching was done, it errored, and then failed bringing EPMA down.  SSHIS advises that Microsoft do not recommend having SQL databases in an AG group and for EPMA, the reporting SQL db is in the AG.  This was raised previously on the build of the infrastructure and SSHIS were told by Optum that it needs to be in there.  When SSHIS runs the scripts automatically, it appears to be failing and bringing down EPMA.
 
Is it possible please to setup a call with Optum specialists and SSHIS, to look at the interdependencies and what can be done to resolve this issue, otherwise, there is a risk this could happen monthly or when the patches are released.


Is it that they are doing both servers at the same time and whilst it is patching it goes down? If so, I believe most sites do the SQL updates manually rather than through an automatic script. As part of this process they should be removing one of the SQL servers from the HA and patching it whilst it is not in the HA. Adding it back to the HA and then removing the other one so that can be patched.

