10/10/2025 11:06:09 - Ian Holden (Work notes)
Hi

oh ok interesting. So that could be one of 2 things, firstly the patches we installed like you said, or it could be just the fact we failed the databases over and both servers where rebooted as part of the patching cycle.

So maybe if your have issues in the future like that maybe worth thinking about failing over the database and rebooting the servers.

Just for your understanding our process is

Manually move all databases onto SQL1.

We then patch SQL2 and reboot it.

We move all databases onto SQL2.

We then patch SQL1 and reboot it.

Final part is moving Test/Train databases back onto SQL2.

On Wednesday these are the patches that where installed

 

Hope that helps

thanks

Spencer




