05/11/2025 09:24:18 - Ian Holden (Work notes)
awaiting access to continue investigation

08/10/2025 10:00:15 - Ian Holden (Work notes)
Mark H. There appears to be two questions here. 1. Differences in display between test and Live, which is correct?. 2. Creation of an immediate dose prompt appears to be inappropriate. It looks like the first attachment ""Afibercept"" comes from their live account. Whereas the ""Afibercept 2"" is screen shots from their test account. Is that how you read it?
 
Regarding the differences in the display, Their test account works the way I would have expected i.e ""SUS"" displays in the admin record only on the days a dose would fall due. Looking at the first set of screen shots from live, I wonder whether the steps to reproduce are the same. Live looks wrong However It looks like they may have suspended immediately after prescribing whereas on Test they recorded a non administration before suspending. Might be worth clarifying the steps to reproduce.
 
Regarding the creation of an immediate dose prompt on unsuspend. This looks wrong and would be the more significant safety concern. This would be the correct behavior for a ""when required - PRN"" prescription but not for a regular scheduled prescription. Might be worth some more onsite testing with a different drug and also different frequencies to assess the scope of the issue and to rule out data issues.
 
Let me know if you want a chat about it

06/10/2025 15:14:44 - Ian Holden (Work notes)
Grace meeting:
check behaviour when suspending as to which options are being selected. reach out to Mark H regards the dose prompt being created when un-suspended

30/09/2025 13:17:01 - Azeem Parvez (Work notes)
Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem -

See Attached Doc called 'Aflibercept 2.docx'. When an item on the drug chart with a frequency of every 6 weeks is added the next dose prompt is added correctly (After 6 weeks). When the drug is suspended, the SUS only shows on the dose prompts. However, when the item is unsuspended the dose prompts are not appearing every 6 weeks and shows available straight away. This behaviour is happening on test

If the same steps are repeated on the live environment the results differ slightly. When the item is suspended it shows sus on all the days as suppose to the dose prompts. System seems to be creating an additional dose prompt when unsuspending the item. 

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? - n/a

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) - none

Look to include screenshots where possible - See attached

Details of the system configuration (region/organisation etc.) - n/a

Details on the user or user type reporting the issue -n/a

Machine specific or full hardware estate impacted e.g. Printing failure for all or one specific user/machine? -none

Details on any relevant data condition (organisation/user/patient/system) -n/a

Clinical Safety / Security / Information Governance Risk -Clinical safety 

Clinical Safety / Information Governance statement -Potential extra dose can be given

Workaround offered or provided –none

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - see attached screenshots

A clear set of recreation steps -Drug chart > Add item with frequency of every 6 weeks > Suspend item and then unsuspend.

