SOAP data to MIG

12/09/2025 10:10:39 - Michael Carter (Work notes)
Swati asked if it's the same as that PRB which I've said no and the PRB is closed so can't be linked to. 

GP DataViewer works like this:
 
1) they select a patient on the front end.
2) we build a SOAP message
3) we send the SOAP message to the MIG which is a company called HealthCare Gateway who EMIS bought out 2 years ago so are now on teams.
4) The MIG sends to a team in Hosted and it pulls 2 records in the same way it does for EMIS Web (Can't remember the name of the 2 records; I think one of them is Patient Summary)
5) the 2 records then make their way back to use though the steps and we display it on screen
 
Lots of ways that lengthy process can go wrong
 
but should get some clues as to where in the Event Viewer following the same steps for that 2nd patient you have screen printed.

