Good morning Mark,
Hope you are good 
 
Would you be able to advise me on the Berkshire customer query regarding case CS1648555 when you have a couple of minutes?
They are currently on version 10.23 and have configured the Inactivity Timeout feature. However, they’re reporting that it doesn’t seem to be working as expected for some users or in certain situations. I’ve already asked them to test whether the password prompt appears after a period of inactivity, and they confirmed that it does work as expected in that regard.
That said, they’re still experiencing issues where patient records remain locked, even when the user has not interacted with the PC for an extended period. From my understanding, the system should automatically release any open records after the user has been inactive for the configured timeout period, but this doesn’t seem to be happening consistently.
Could you help me answer the following?
 
1.How is the Inactivity Timeout function expected to work?
2.What could be the reasons it’s not working as expected in some cases?
3.Are there any known scenarios or exceptions where the Inactivity Timeout might not trigger or release locks as intended?
 
I will attach below documents of some example and their testing's 
 
Thanks in advance for your help!

