Hi

Thank you for the phone call this afternoon.

We are looking to trial the use of the eMM module to enable the dispensing of patient specific medicines without printing off requests from our EPMA system

A Trust we work closely with (Calderdale and Huddersfield) are already using this.

We have had a look at the roles and permissions but we do not appear to have all the permissions we need to undertake this work.

The two missing permission appear to be:
eMM dispensing worklist
eMM dispensing

we also have which are different from the one used at Calderdale and Huddersfield:
eMM PMR (pharmacist) and eMM PMR (technician) – Calderdale and Huddersfield use eMM Pharmacist &L3 Tech – we understand it is possible to rename if needed so wondered if these would show the same information

This is the process used at the other Trust which we would like to be able to follow:

Add item from EPR to EMIS. Add supply request and if pharmacist then also use clinical check button.
 


If ordered by a technician go to eMM clinical checking, click on patient then click eMM PMR (pharmacist), then clinical check button.
 
 

In dispensary, click on the worklist  - which we don’t have
 


then on eMM dispensing – which we don’t have

We will also need : 
Accuracy checking,

