Just a heads up to inform you that our EMIS change request regarding performance issues has been approved by our Trust change advisory group.

2 weeks ago, I asked colleagues (especially within Procurement, who were experiencing the majority of the item enquiry issues) to inform me if they had issues with item enquiry / client loading speeds / general performance issues. To my surprise, the procurement team told me that they were no longer experiencing the above issues, and wider staff did not report any issues.

I have reached out to our IT department to ask them if any changes have been made to the network /  if any patches have been applied / if any new windows updates have been deployed, which would have lead to this performance improvement - currently awaiting a response.

For now, I think it would be wise to park the change request whilst I ascertain with IT if they may have had any impact. Does this work for you all?

Thanks,

Brad

