Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem -Duplicates are showing in interface Ap files.

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -All sites

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -error messages attached

Message
Executed as user: CUMBRIA-RNN\SQLAGTsvcNCICSQLSL01. Could not find server 'NCIC-EMIS-REP\PHARMACY' in sys.servers. Verify that the correct server name was specified. If necessary, execute the stored procedure sp_addlinkedserver to add the server to sys.servers. [SQLSTATE 42000] (Error 7202).  The step failed. 


Look to include screenshots where possible -attached 

Details of the system configuration (region/organisation etc.) -no
Details on the user or user type reporting the issue -genfin Users

Machine specific or full hardware estate impacted e.g. Printing failure for all or one specific user/machine? -

Details on any relevant data condition (organisation/user/patient/system) -

Clinical Safety / Security / Information Governance Risk -No

Clinical Safety / Information Governance statement -NA

Workaround offered or provided –Ian setup a job to prevent duplication Which seems disabled.


What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - 
I have investigated and tried to find the duplicate. And checked the availability groups I have checked the reconcile status as well


A clear set of recreation steps -
-I suspected this is mapping/configuration issue 

--- Detect if this instance's role is a Primary Replica.
-- If this instance's role is NOT a Primary Replica stop the job so that it does not go on to the next job step
DECLARE @rc int; 
EXEC @rc = master.dbo.fn_hadr_group_is_primary N'NCICSQLAG01';---------------lisners

IF @rc = 0
BEGIN;
    DECLARE @name sysname;
    SELECT  @name = (SELECT name FROM msdb.dbo.sysjobs WHERE job_id = CONVERT(uniqueidentifier, $(ESCAPE_NONE(JOBID))));
    
    EXEC msdb.dbo.sp_stop_job @job_name = @name;
    PRINT 'Stopped the job since this is not a Primary Replica';
END;


2: DECLARE @Batch INT
DECLARE @Date VARCHAR(8)

