I can pick this up on the 17th November on my return, if this is something that can be placed on hold. 
 
In saying this, the Proxys cannot be removed from the servers as this goes against the new hardening policies and the increased security that is required.
As such, we would require and ask for further information to support this reasoning, but please note that we can add URL’s and Endpoints to the proxy whitelisting that may be required to help support products and their connectivity.
 
As you have outlined the 2 required Ascribe servers, we can ask Security to Whitelist the DSS web url for these two servers.
 
@Janette Onen to assist security, could you confirm the following:
 
•	Is this Platform Proxy Aware? – Can it use the Servers WinHTTP setting or can it be setup in a config file to use a Proxy?
•	What URLS specifically are required for the Drug Database to be updated?
 
@James Warren would you mind reviewing this information and confirm if it would be possible to whitelist the URLS?
I have had confirmation from Patrick Lynch (Service Owner) that the Drug Database for Ascribe is not being automatically updated due to this problem.

