Good Morning Emily,
 
I hope you are well.
 
I am reaching out from the Telefonica Tech managed service side, who manage the Servers that Ascribe resides on.
I've had a read over the original Incident and the Request that Megan has raised about EMIS ascribe not downloading queued updates & Unable to download new products onto EMIS for over 1 month.
 
From what I gather it was reported back from the DSS Team that there needs to be some amendments on the IE Mode and Trusted sites according to the documentation that was supplied.
We are having some trouble confirming where this needs to be applied.
 
Would it be possible for you to outline:
 
•	Is this for Server side?
o	If so, can you outline which server? (as there are 8 for Ascribe service that we host)
 
•	Is this for Workstation side?
o	I have tested this on a workstation, and this looks like it is navigating without us making any changes, so can we please have some elaboration on what is required?
 
I have included Chris Hill from Optum, in the event you are off, so we can get this directed to a different Optum member of staff.
 
Note:
If a product is in 'Live Operation', we do not permit automatic updates to products without this going through CUH/TT Change Control.
As a result, could we please get more information to ascertain if this is actual software Updates (Version uplifts) or what specifically this is updating.
 
Kind Regards,
 
Ian Harte	

