09/10/2025 10:17:52 - Sean Prescott (Work notes)
Case originally logged under CS1622913 which went to the optum help centre team assigned to Phillip LAmie

Kamlesh asked me to look into the issue to see if we can advise or help further on Monday 6th October

Customer was basically asking if there are any settings with the pharmacy software for printing that can change the temperature setting on the ZD420 Label printers due to labels smudging when coming into contact with moisture / water

After some initial investigation on our software and the label printers themselves, I deemed the issue to be with the label printer software or Drivers as I was unable to find anything in the Optum software that would affect the printing out software simply prints to the printer it told to print to

First check i did was ask for a photo of one of the labels that has come into contact with water. (attached is lebelsmudge.jpg)

trust advised me the label printed normally then it was dipped in water and smudged.

I then advised the trust to look at the driver settings as this is where the setting for the printer are.

The printer was a direct thermal and set up as such.

I asked what the type of media being used as label paper it was direct thermal not thermal transfer paper

it was direct thermal.

i then asked which type of direct thermal as there are 3 types

Type 1: Standard (Uncoated) Direct Thermal Paper
 
Type 2: Top-Coated Direct Thermal Paper (Synthetic Option)
 
Type 3: Waterproof Synthetic Direct Thermal Labels

They responded with head office said it was type 1 uncoated.

I have suggested that they used type 2 / type 3. 

Type 2 is coated a moisture resistant but not water proof.
Type 3 is coated and is waterproof a suitable for in a fridge or freezer.

They have agreed to this and are ordering new label types.

Trust have advised they use pre printed labels with their address on and warning to keep out of reach of children.

They will use the blank label when they come but needed the address changing which they managed to do but need to warning on the template.

I advised to edit the label as they did with the address - to free text type it at the bottom where the pre printed label would have the address. as they are using blank labels the warning coulf fit at the bottom.

Once they have the pre printed labels with their specific data on it including the warning. they can then remove this line from the template so it then appears as before but now on the correct label material for a fridge/freezer and is waterproof.

