26/11/2025 09:46:52 - Kiu Hong Adrian Wong (Work notes)
This case is about EIE certificates, Swati has reached out to me for help with this. Adding note on here for full visibility, in case she requires any further assistance. 
Though, hopefully this provides more information for Swati to take next steps. 

Cert - 'Berkshire EMIS Conexes TEST' 
OLD thumbprint ends with - 561dd9
NEW thumbprint ends with - 4e4c83

This cert is provided by Servelec. 

They have already provided the new cert and it has been added onto the UAT EIE boxes already. (manage computer certificates> personal)
EMEUW2UT02EIE05.awshosted.emis-clinical.com
EMEUW2UT02EIE06.awshosted.emis-clinical.com

Check 1:
After the cert was added, I checked whether the new thumprint needed to be added to the Interface Engine Configuration tool -IECT (for both PAS and eDischarge)
I did this by comparing the OLD thumbprint to what is in the IECT
i.e. C:\InterfaceEngine\Test\ITKADTPMI and C:\InterfaceEngine\Test\eDischarge
Loading as admin > going into the EIE component settings tab and selecting either IPReceiver for PAS or IPTransmitter for eDischarge. 

Result 1: 
The old thumbprint matched only the eDischarge thumbprint. Therefore this certificate is ONLY for eDischarge. 
-- PAS uses a different thumbprint (ending with 57763). This doesn't expire until 20/01/2026 - which is soon, but something for another case. 

Leela/Access has been mentioning:
'10.125.33.221:16010'  port 16010, if you check the setting table 
Select top 100 * from Setting WHERE [key] like '%port%'
You will see that IPReceiver (PAS) is port 16010. Which has nothing to do with this cert. This case is about eDischarge. 

Therefore we know that the customer is getting PAS, eDischarge mixed up. 

Suggested next steps:
- Clarify to the customer that the certificate isn't for PAS, its for eDischarge and the transmission of messages from Optum > Access, via PORT 16010. 
- Sync with the customer, maybe they amended the config for PAS, thinking the cert had expired and should have amended eDischarge instead. 
- Once the config is correct on both sides (should be fine on our end). We and the customer should both do a eDischarge/PAS restart and see whether messages flow again.

