Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem -

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? - 28/10/2025

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) - N/A
Look to include screenshots where possible - N/A

Details on the user or user type reporting the issue - the user is unable to progress past the initial item selection on the patient record, the system is halting at the point we should be selecting the required raw materials and then generating the worksheet and labels. 

Machine specific or full hardware estate impacted e.g. Printing failure for all or one specific user/machine? - N/A

Details on any relevant data condition (organisation/user/patient/system) - N/A

Clinical Safety / Security / Information Governance Risk - N/A

Clinical Safety / Information Governance statement - N/A

Workaround offered or provided – Yes / No - no

Have you followed all of the steps of the workaround provided on PRB - Yes / No - yes

Does the current workaround work - Yes / No
--If No selected from above state reason why not working and provide screenshots of the errors.

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used -
Have asked nick for the help , 
After investigation this is working as designed. Manufacturing batch numbers were added to the system as automated sequential generated number in the year 2000 with the format MAmmddnnnn where

M = Manufacuring batch number, A is the year 2000 through to Z at 2025, then it changes to a for 2026 through to z in 2052, This provides a 56 year roll round on unique batch numbers for a stockholding.

The customer is unable to generate a worksheet

