14/01/2026 10:30:32 - Michael Carter (Work notes)
Hi,

Yes, need more information. 

1)	Are the terminals VDI’s? (Virtual Desktop Infrastructure) as in the name changes each time you log onto them.
2)	Are you attempting to put multiple terminals onto the same line in Terminal Activation desktop? Eg. If you have a location on “Terminal Activation”  like ""AAD-SHARED-1"" then on “Device1” you select it. Then on “Device2” you also select “AAD-SHARED-1” this will kick “Device1” off.
3)	Can you create a step-by-step word document with screenprints to show the problem? With the following details:
a)	Image of the full “Terminal Activation” desktop
b)	Name of the terminal you are on.
c)	Which location you have selected in the “Terminal Activation” desktop.
d)	After restarting the computer, go back to the “Terminal Activation” desktop and ensure that you can still see the same Domain Name/Computer Name at the top. Also, that if you look at the location you activated onto does it still show your Domain Name/Computer Name on it?

Few bits of feedback from reading the case/emails:

There is no limit to the number of terminals you can have or the number of ones you can activate. It is however one computer per each of the locations on the Terminal Activation window. 

Terminals work like this:

They are Locations that you have created in the Pharmacy Location Editor. When you select one in the Terminal Activation desktop it updates the DB’s Terminal table for that LocationID with the DomainName, ComputerName and Cookie (The 16-digit code at the top). When you login to the software it looks at the Terminal table to see if has an entry with the same DomainName, ComputerName. If it doesn’t find one, it will look to see if it has one with the same Cookie. 

Kind Regards,

Michael

