15/12/2025 12:15:19 - Gunjan Idnani (Work notes)
I have been testing in our pharmacy and found that:

Core Issues
When the software is reinstalled on a desktop PC or surface pro device & configured to point to the correct FQDN server name.  Then found on Ascribe, Activated and Rebooted it will load and allow staff members to log in. 

However, the issue we have found is actually linked to the number of devices which can be activated concurrently. As when I installed and activate on a 3rd test device this worked on the new device however then removed the activation from the first of 2 test PC's I reinstalled & activated on.

When looking from Ascribe as logged in by a system admin account (Madeline) , I have found the software have over 100 devices added which have been removed from our network and over 70 of these are still activated. When we have tried to delete these entries to resolve what I believe is the overarching issue the staff do not have permissions to do so. Is this something you would do from your end or can they be given permission / access to deactivate & delete assets which are now disposed of to purge the system?

I believe when these are removed this will free up enough licences for them to have every Pharmacy device (70 - 80 in total) all activated concurrently and clear their overarching issues.

Below is a Screenshot of the Assets, as you can see any Device Starting with CZC was removed from our network over 2 years ago due to trust wide Hardware refreshes / a change to our computer naming conventions:


We are also experiencing the following issues from within the system can you provide guidance / solution to these issues also:

