04/12/2025 11:49:35 - Gunjan Idnani (Work notes)
On multiple devices where errors have been identified, I have removed the existing install of the Ascribe software, rebooted and reinstalled as per the advised resolution.

In the Location – C:\Ascribe\Smartclient\Configuration I have checked and as part of the reinstall, updated the client configuration to point to 
VIR-PHARM-01.gmw.nhs.uk rather than VIR-PHARM-01

 
This has then worked on the first attempt, however, fails thereafter with the same error message, I have then worked with Cyber to assess the logs and found the software configuration was still set to VIR-PHARM-01.gmw.nhs.uk, however will not load. The logs show that the software defaulted back to VIR-PHARM-01 which is not the FQDN so therefore cannot be resolved in iBoss. 

As a brief background on this, we are migrating from an On-Premises Domain (GMW) to a Web based Azure domain (GMMH), iBoss is the security platform which manages all of our devices. So therefore all software needs to be complaint with this and if not we need to find a way to make sure these can speak with each other.

So for our perspective can this be escalated internally to help up find a resolution, as 2 possible solutions which we could implement very readily would be one of the below options:

1????Is there a specific entry in the registry or a dll file which designates / points to the server which we could edit this to point to the FQDN?

2????Would it be possible to recreate the MSI file we use to install the Ascribe software which by default points to the FQDN instead?

3????Or another solution which you may be able to provide

I am happy to work with what is the best / easiest  approach to find a solution, as the next step will be to turn this (when working as expected) with our new domain and iBoss into a package which we can deploy via group policy management / our self-service portal.

