A clear description of the Problem - Template permissions are altering/resetting weekly.

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? - Over a years.

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) - No error

Look to include screenshots where possible - attached

Details of the system configuration (region/organisation etc.) - 10.23

Details on the user or user type reporting the issue - The prescibers

Machine specific or full hardware estate impacted e.g. Printing failure for all or one specific user/machine? - NA

Details on any relevant data condition (organisation/user/patient/system) - NA

Clinical Safety / Security / Information Governance Risk - No

Clinical Safety / Information Governance statement - No

Workaround offered or provided – No (No workaround)

Have you followed all of the steps of the workaround provided on PRB - No

Does the current workaround work -  No
--If No selected from above state reason why not working and provide screenshots of the errors.

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge-based articles have you used? I have checked for hidden roles that might override the permission, and I couldn't find any. And asked the DSS team, and they said they only set whether the product can be templated or not, and they don't change permission on the template.
