Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem -

Trust is unable to add a message of the day without error 403 forbidden appearing

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -

sinec being upgraded to 10.23

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -

403 - Forbidden: access is denied.

You do not have permission to view this directory or page using the credentials that you supplied

Look to include screenshots where possible -

see 

EMIS MOTD Error.png and cs1692608.docx

Workaround offered or provided – Yes 

if you add a message of the day without a hyperlink in the message it works, but the hyperlink is required in the message of the day to be clickable.

Have you followed all of the steps of the workaround provided on PRB - No

there is no prb for this

Does the current workaround work - Yes 

yes but as stated above the link needs to be clickable

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - 

See cs1692608.docx

the issue is with ModSecurity blocking Hyperlinks

online it said this

it said this

Why It Happened
•	The OWASP Core Rule Set (CRS) is designed to prevent XSS attacks.
•	Rule 941150 blocks HTML attributes like href, style, src in user input.

So this is something to do with rule 941150 in modsecurity blocking an actual URL / Hyperlink being added

Looking at event view Modsecurity is blocking quite a few URL's

NOTE: i did refer the customer back to their IT but after speakign with Ian apparently ModSecurity is part of 10.23

I tried to recreate thus on United Lincs but he message of the day accepted the message with a hyperlink in it.


A clear set of recreation steps -

1) Open message of the day editor
2) Give the message of the day template a name
3) Paste link: e.g. https://www.blackcountryformulary.nhs.uk/default.asp
4) Assign it to relevant roles. 
5) Click ok / save.

Below error appears.

Server Error 
403 - Forbidden: Access is denied. 
You do not have permission to view this directory or page using the credentials that you supplied.

---

if you do the same thing with just plain text no hyperlinks it will create

