04/12/2025 15:48:37 - Michael Carter (Work notes)
Will take this to Grace and ask permission to send the following draft email:

""Dear Jonathan,

Thank you for bringing the issue to our attention regarding order numbers being mixed between PSO and non-PSO orders, which results in errors during the receiving process.

After reviewing the situation, we’ve identified that this behaviour occurs within the current (legacy) Stores module. As you may know, we are in the process of a revitalization project to replace the old code in this module. Because of this, any fix to the existing version would require a new release of the legacy code, which is not planned.

For this reason, we recommend moving to the new Stores module and verifying whether the issue persists there. The new module has been redesigned to address several limitations of the old system, and this may resolve the problem you’re experiencing.

Additionally, we are working closely with our Product team to clarify how customers can transition to the new Stores module outside of having an active upgrade project. We will share more details with you as soon as we have a clear path forward.

Please let us know if you would like to discuss the next steps or have any questions in the meantime.

Best regards,

Michael Carter

Associate Tech Support Analyst
""

