Change required

03/12/2025 09:19:40 - Sean Prescott (Work notes)
Ran this

declare @locationid int
set @locationid = 22

select productstockid, * from wproduct where productstockid in (
select productstockid from productstock ps
where ps.locationid_site = @locationid
and ps.stocktakestatus = 1
and ps.productstockid not in
(select productstockid from wproduct where siscode in
(select distinct(nsvcode) from wstocktake where locationid_site = @locationid
and status in (0,1))))
order by siscode

Found 1107 products on a stock take.

but from front end will not reset the product file.

front end shows 1107 SQL Above shows the 1107 products on a stock take status 1 

I will reset this via sql with following sql script

declare @locationid int
set @locationid = 22

begin tran
update productstock
set stocktakestatus = 0
where productstockid in (
select productstockid from wproduct where productstockid in (
select productstockid from productstock ps
where ps.locationid_site = @locationid
and ps.stocktakestatus = 1
and ps.productstockid not in
(select productstockid from wproduct where siscode in
(select distinct(nsvcode) from wstocktake where locationid_site = @locationid
and status in (0,1)))))
--Rollback
--commit

