06/01/2026 13:57:08 - Michael Carter (Work notes)
Problem Summary

This Problem relates to inaccuracies within the EPMA “Omitted Dose Report”, specifically the “Doses Not Actioned” section at the bottom of the report.

Initially, the bottom section of the report was found to be displaying dose data from future dates, which was incorrect. Following investigation, Michael (Support) identified and corrected the logic used in this section. As part of the remediation, a new report named “Doses Not Recorded V3” was created to correctly represent this dataset.

The Midlands Partnership were advised of this change and confirmed they could continue using the original Omitted Dose Report, provided they ignore the bottom “Doses Not Actioned” section and instead use “Doses Not Recorded V3” to view that information.

Subsequently, the Essex Partnership raised a similar issue and were also provided with the “Doses Not Recorded V3” report. However, Essex later advised that the report was showing more missed doses than expected.

Further investigation by Michael identified that the report was including doses which no longer exist in the live system. An example case showed a patient admitted between 12?Nov?2025 and 16?Dec?2025. When running the report for 22?Dec?2025 to 31?Dec?2025, the patient appeared to have 44 missed doses, with the last recorded date being 25?Dec?2025. Reviewing the live EPMA system confirmed that these doses had since been removed and no longer exist.

The suspected cause is that the patient episode remained open until 25?Dec?2025 and was later closed, resulting in the Event Engine deleting the associated dose records that were after the end date of 16-Dec-2025. However, those deleted dose records remain present in the EPMA Reporting Database, causing the report to display obsolete data that no longer reflects the live system state.

