IH
Ian Holden
Additional comments•27/01/2026 15:59:28
Hi Arif
can you confirm that the printer has been checked as follows:

1. Windows Spooling Settings
Windows may be set to ""Spool documents"" which delays each label.

Go to Control Panel ? Devices & Printers
Right?click the Zebra printer ? Printer Properties
Open the Advanced tab
Change:

? Print directly to the printer
? Uncheck Enable advanced printing features




2. Wrong Driver Installed (ZebraDriver vs ZDesigner)
For thermal printers, using a generic driver makes printing slow and ""rasterized.""
Install the correct driver
Download & install the Zebra ZDesigner driver for your exact model:

ZD420, GK420d, ZD220, etc. all need the matching ZDesigner V5/V6 driver.

After installing, remove the old printer and re-add it using the Zebra installer.


3. Mode Mismatch (ZPL vs EPL vs Line Mode)
If your label format is meant for ZPL, but the printer is set to Line Mode, the print job becomes extremely slow.
Fix

Print a configuration report (usually hold FEED button on power?up)
Check the Command Language:

Should be ZPL (or EPL, depending on your label software)

If wrong:

Use Zebra Setup Utilities to change the mode
? Printer Tools ? Command Language ? ZPL


4. USB Power or Cable Issues
A failing USB cable or port can cause slow or delayed transfer.

Use a short USB cable (?2m)
Try a different USB port
Avoid USB hubs — plug into PC directly


5. Label Size / Darkness / Speed Settings
If speed or darkness settings are too high, the printer throttles itself.

Use Zebra Setup Utilities ? Printer Settings:

Print Speed: 4–6 ips (recommended)
Darkness: 10–15 (varies by model)
Resolution: Match printer (203dpi / 300dpi)

best regards
Ian

