30/03/2026 13:15:17 - Michael Carter (Work notes)
Hi all,

I’ve reviewed the incident on the 26th while I was on leave and can confirm it exhibits the same behaviour as previously described.

We’ve now completed investigations across all reported periods, including review of SQL deadlock reports, SQL and application logs, Windows Event Viewer, and component configuration. There are no errors or failures observed within the platform.

From our perspective, the consistent behaviour is that inbound messaging from PAS stops. We are not seeing failed processing, rejected messages, or any attempts reaching our system.

At this stage, we don’t have any further diagnostic information to provide from our side. We’re happy to attend a call if helpful, however we wouldn’t have new findings to present; any further progress would need to focus on PAS/interface behaviour upstream, particularly around send and retry handling. I know it creates a new connection for each message, but does it do the same on a retry attempt, or does it fall over when it comes to retry attempts?

If additional evidence becomes available showing outbound attempts or errors during the affected periods, we’re happy to review it.

Kind Regards,

Michael

