26/02/2026 10:15:36 - Karen Gettins (Work notes)
Info received from Mark H 

Karen

I've been reviewing CS1726012 this afternoon and Swati has updated the case. However,  Michael Carter subsequently found an old PRB which is the same issue PRB0048707 . This was assessed as a very low clinical risk at the time and closed in 2022. The issue has existed as far back as version 10.19, so is very old.  An idea for an enhancement was added to Aha https://emisgroup.aha.io/ideas/ideas/MEDSMAN2-I-72  This has not been brought forward into development and is very unlikely to be brought forward until modernisation of ePMA.

Berkshire are arguing that this should be revisited and regarded as PRB rather than an enhancement. However it would be very unlikely to be brought forward into development even so as the PRB backlog is also very long, so it's a rather academic argument. 

Mark

