"CS1735054","Nottingham University Hospitals NHS Trust","4 - Low","13/02/2026 11:29:23","In Progress","Added contract prices dropping off","29/07/2026 08:10:42","jessica.thacker2@nhs.net","Acute Care Medicines Management Level 2 Team","Michael Carter","21/07/2026 11:28:44 - Michael Carter (Work notes)
To see if a contract is Active or not:

DECLARE @dtWorkingDate DATETIME = GETDATE();

SELECT
    WExtraDrugDetailID,
    DateOfChange,
    NewStopDate,
    DateUpdated,
    NewContractNumber,
    NewContractPrice,
    CASE
        WHEN @dtWorkingDate >= CONVERT(DATETIME, ISNULL(DateOfChange,''),103)
         AND @dtWorkingDate <= CONVERT(DATETIME, ISNULL(NewStopDate,''),103)
        THEN 'ACTIVE'
        ELSE 'NOT ACTIVE'
    END AS ContractStatus
FROM WExtraDrugDetail
WHERE NSVCode = '<NSV>'
ORDER BY WExtraDrugDetailID DESC;

On a test environment need to add in the detail that they are doing and then see if thinks it's active.

