Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem - Trust was testing the Tie messaging 

Our TIE will be down for 2 hours on the 24th of Feb 2026 from 08:00 to 10:00, this will cause a backlog of messages form the PAS, we plan to test the message throttling we have currently set for this, during that time, when the messages start to flow across the link again. we are currently set to 100p/m, we will slowly throttle up to  150 then 200 then 250, to see how the system copes. this is advance warning of the work we are planning, to make you aware that there will be down time and possible issues seen at those times.

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -

After taking the tie down the started to test the throttling at 150 200 and 300 to see how the system copes.

Messages were built up but system couldn't cope with the amount of messages being pushed through all at once.

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -

No errors just system could cope and process the messages fast enough

Look to include screenshots where possible -

no screen shots

Workaround offered or provided – No

There is no workaround they were advised that the system / servers and memory needs to be upgraded they have done this its made no effect

Have you followed all of the steps of the workaround provided on PRB - No

No workaround and no prb

Does the current workaround work - No
--If No selected from above state reason why not working and provide screenshots of the errors.

They have upgraded their system and memory but its made not difference they can only have the throttling at 120 they are expecting to be able to throttle to 300 messages a minute

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - 

we monitored the messages. messages were moving and did not get stuck

A clear set of recreation steps -

Stop the TIE interface for a couple of hours increase throttling gradually from 100 to 300. Stan reports the system could not cope beyond 120 without the entries system going very slow.

Stan advised the sweet spot for the server currently is 120 - 125. the issue was processing of messages which was taking a long time to do.

Stan also advised the 120 - 125 is slower than their old servers which was set at 150.

Something else is not allowing the messages to process fast enough. And requires PA to investigate

