"CS1748622","Northern Care Alliance NHS Foundation Trust","4 - Low","10/03/2026 15:35:53","Closed","Warning ( 5 &25 )","17/03/2026 16:51:30","aidan.magee@nca.nhs.uk","Acute Care Medicines Management Level 1 Team","Muhammed Rashik Rahman","","Core Pharmacy","17/03/2026 16:51:30","","8",""
"CS1748632","The Royal Wolverhampton NHS Trust","3 - Medium","10/03/2026 15:43:32","Closed","Error with Windows 11 update 24H2","30/03/2026 11:46:02","system","Acute Care Medicines Management Level 2 Team","Michael Carter","11/03/2026 09:05:34 - Sean Prescott (Work notes)
Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem -

There is an issue when upgrading from win 11 23H2 to 24H2 with this install file it doesn't register come up with the below error.  Do we have a contact from EPMA (vendor) to get some guidance to what the issue could be?  When we rebuild to 24H2 the install files works fine but we cant be rebuilding all pc's due to this file not installing so can we ask for advice/guidance from vendor why its not installing when upgrading to 24H2 to from 23H2?

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -

10/03/26 - Trying to upgrade or build a laptop on 23h2 to 24h2

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -

See attachment Standard error for this issue

Look to include screenshots where possible -

See attachements

Workaround offered or provided – Yes from PRB0052991 

Have you followed all of the steps of the workaround provided on PRB - Yes 

Trust advise they have followed all instructions

Does the current workaround work - No

See attachement

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - 

PRB0052991  with workaround of

Workaround
 Running the installer
Ask sites to add ctl3d32.dll into the SysWOW folder (This needs to be copied from a PC that has not had the windows update)
Run the installer (which should now run successfully)
Crystal Reports (Stocktake print) should work as expected
Using the application
Ask sites to add ctl3d32.dll into the SysWOW folder (This needs to be copied from a PC that has not had the windows update)
Crystal Reports (Stocktake print) should work as expected
 

A clear set of recreation steps -

Customer says this does not work and wants a proper fix.

""
Unfortunately this workaround only addresses issues with ctl3d32.dll - we are having issues with craxddrt.dll.
This file is present in both 23h2 and 24h2 but for whatever reason it fails to register, not entirely sure what that means. We have tried copying the same file from 23h2 to 24h2 but we still get this same error. The only way to resolve this was to rebuild Windows on the PC, but this is not a feasible workaround at all as we cannot do this for every device that encounters this problem.
""

Customer no longer wants to perform a full rebuild when an upgrade should be working


