Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

--A clear description of the Problem -

The trust is unable to amend the Directions on a label when it is on the Medical or AICU ward and set to Discharge

when they change the direction then go to print it, it reverts back to the original text

This doesn't happen on other wards

--Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -

08/04/2026 15:03:27

--Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -

No error messages

--Look to include screenshots where possible -

See MEDI directions.jpg

I will send the email which contains the videos showing it working on other wards and video showing it not working on the medical ward

Direction on line is twice a day. they amend it to once a day when printing it reverts back to twice a day

--Workaround offered or provided – No

--Have you followed all of the steps of the workaround provided on PRB - No

There is no PRB

--Does the current workaround work - No
--If No selected from above state reason why not working and provide screenshots of the errors.

There is no PRB

--What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - 

There is no KB or PRB on this

--A clear set of recreation steps -

It seems to only happen on Medical ward and when its dispense other wards this works as expected.

I have 2 videos from the customer but they will not attach on this case or open via email due to optum restrictions.
It can be sent to a personal email and played on a non optum device. I will send those in the email when i send the information that this has been passed up

Patient Hosp number 6128968
The select the line of a patient on the medical ward.
Cetrizine 10mg oral once a day
click dispense
edit the label direction to show Three times a day
print
it pops up three times a day in the list select to print then it reverts back to once a day in the list.

If this is done on any other ward then it will work as expected.

