07/05/2026 11:37:46 - Muhammed Rashik Rahman (Work notes)
Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem - the system goes to outages for sometimes with they receive  Long standing SPID Report 

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? - this is ongoing issue for sometime not sure when this started happening. However, I have attached previous cases related to this in the case note.

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) - attached normal Error ID showing in the front and  the details are traceable in the  logs.

Look to include screenshots where possible - Attached

Details of the system configuration (region/organisation etc.) - NA

Details on the user or user type reporting the issue - All users 

Machine specific or full hardware estate impacted e.g. Printing failure for all or one specific user/machine? - Live DB servers

Details on any relevant data condition (organisation/user/patient/system) - NA

Clinical Safety / Security / Information Governance Risk -NA

Clinical Safety / Information Governance statement -No

Workaround offered or provided – No (But they can log case with us to kill the session if the outage is going for a long time)

Have you followed all of the steps of the workaround provided on PRB - No

Does the current workaround work - Yes 
--If No selected from above state reason why not working and provide screenshots of the errors.

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - I have reviewed the indexing and confirmed that it is appropriate, with no recommendations for index rebuild or alteration. The scheduled job is running as expected. Although no alerts have been triggered recently, the customer would like to understand why this issue continues to occur intermittently. At this stage, an exact root cause has not been identified.
The attached report received via email shows that the issue is predominantly related to the Session table being locked by the stored procedure [icwsys].[pUserLoginShared]. The issue is sporadic and not linked to any specific functional area. There is no consistent pattern for alert generation, as the alerts occur at varying times—sometimes around midnight and at other times in the morning.


A clear set of recreation steps - No replication steps. can run the long running query as in the job already scheduled.

