"CS1777735","Berkshire Healthcare NHS Foundation Trust","4 - Low","05/05/2026 14:59:05","In Progress","CS1741460/ePMA Business Continuity Plan also in relation to CS1694944/ePMA Business Continuity Plan","22/07/2026 17:05:04","Karen.Gettins@emishealth.com","Acute Care Medicines Management Level 2 Team","Michael Carter","03/06/2026 12:19:21 - Michael Carter (Work notes)
Emailed Leela and Nishfa:

""Hello,
I wanted to provide an update on the issues you raised
regarding the EPMA BC reports.
1. Green ticks and red crosses not displaying

We have investigated this across the three affected pages (When Required,
Regular Scheduled, and Discontinued and Expired) on both report servers. The
behaviour was not always consistent as the reports were sometimes executed
against the secondary server, which did not always preserve the required
formatting. We have updated this on the secondary server also to ensure
consistency across both servers.
2. Font display in PDF outputs

I had a discussion with Graham (cc’d) regarding the work done during the
project. There were no specific changes made for PDF output at the time—only
font adjustments on the three reports mentioned above. We have also tested this
at another site and observed the same behaviour. Based on this, it does not
appear possible to achieve the required formatting within PDF output. As a
result, the recommended approach would be to use the Word document format
instead.

I appreciate that I previously indicated this was working on the server, but
after further testing, this does not appear to be the case.
3. Admin codes display (# + letter codes)

The codes you mentioned (displayed as ‘#’ followed by a letter) are appearing
as designed. There is a key included within each Patient Summary section of the
report explaining these codes (see example below).

Could you please confirm whether there are any other characters not displaying
correctly, or if the concern is limited to the tick/cross symbols and the
hashtag codes?
If there are any more tick/cross symbols, please say which
page they are on eg. When Required medication, Infusion etc.
For reference, the Admin Codes key:
 
Please let me know if you would
like us to review any specific examples or if you have further questions.
Kind regards,
Michael
""

