19/05/2026 13:07:22 - Sean Prescott (Work notes)
advised Swati of following

At first look they are using another system and trying to integrate it with ours.
 
Something called A-PAS - im guessing aspen pas system.
 
Which uses different number from our system.
 
Unless theres somewhere on the patient details to put this extra information im not sure it can be done.
 
As a probable workaround if theres a section in the patient details which could be used for this unique hosp number from another system. that could be used then the print element of that data can be added to the label. (Im guessing on this now).
 
Stuff like Name, address, NHS number, hospital number, age, other.
 
If other exists i can be entered there and the print element for other used for the label
 
one major problem is how does this data get sent into our system from their A-PAS system to our system to populate that field.
The customer wont want to be entering the A-PAS number on every patient manually. Something should be in place that their system sends this data to us.
 
That's just an example off the top of my head of how to do it.
 
Which is basically rubbish, but you get the point.
 
I would think this needs a project and the account manager to ensure this is done properly and efficiently with minimum disruption to what they want.
 
Firstly how will the data from A-PAS be sent to our system and then the label needs the print element adding to it. so it shows our Hospital number and the A-PAS hospital number.
 
I think only a project manager and account manager can answer that.
 
So double check with a PA. and probably mention what ive said to so they understand it better than the notes the customer has put on the case.

