Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem -site generated a stock take in 854 location for CD3, CD4, and CD5 location codes. Usually there is over 100 lines, but yesterday when we generated the report there were only 38. Now when I try and do a stocktake of a single line that was missing from our big CD stocktake, it is saying that there is no data.

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -no

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -no

Look to include screenshots where possible -attached on case (CS1765565) 

Details of the system configuration (region/organisation etc.) -mo

Details on the user or user type reporting the issue -no

Machine specific or full hardware estate impacted e.g. Printing failure for all or one specific user/machine? -no

Details on any relevant data condition (organisation/user/patient/system) -no

Clinical Safety / Security / Information Governance Risk -no

Clinical Safety / Information Governance statement -no

Workaround offered or provided – No

Have you followed all of the steps of the workaround provided on PRB -  No

Does the current workaround work - No
--If No selected from above state reason why not working and provide screenshots of the errors.

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - 

A clear set of recreation steps -

During the meeting, I outlined the following steps for adherence:

1. Begin by conducting a review to identify the current available resources.
2. Following that, perform a 'reset product file' and examine the results for any changes.
3. It is essential to refrain from executing a 'full product reset,' as this will entirely reset the product file for that site.

Although they followed these steps, they are still encountering issues. Upon reviewing the database, everything appears to be in order in both the product stock and stocktake tables. However, when they processed the stocktake, the status changed automatically. I confirmed this with them during our meeting and also informed Ian.

I have already discussed this matter with Ian.

Need More investigation 

Thanks,
swati

