02/06/2026 14:19:55 - Muhammed Rashik Rahman (Work notes)
From Lee Antcliffe
The issue was caused by a historical FinOps IAM role still referenced in the code, which no longer exists in the AWS account. This caused the KMS policy update to fail during deployment.
 
My recent Dynatrace change was unrelated, it just happened to trigger the workflow execution. The underlying problem is attributed to legacy code and reliance on Terraform plans that didn’t surface the risk clearly.

02/06/2026 11:33:12 - Muhammed Rashik Rahman (Work notes)
From Lee Antcliffe
""A scheduled infrastructure update was applied on 1 June 2026 for Dynatrace monitoring. During the deployment, the process failed due to a reference to a non-existent IAM role in a KMS key policy.
 
As a result, load balancer target groups were created but not fully registered, which was identified following customer reporting.
 
The issue was resolved by removing the invalid IAM role reference and re-running the deployment to correctly register the targets. An IIS restart was performed to restore service.""

