29/07/2026 11:02:55 - Sean Prescott (Work notes)
Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

--A clear description of the Problem -

--Trust are reporting a error during the installation of a new machine. This is happening on one machine only

Run-time error-2147467261 (80004003)': Object reference not set to an instance of an object

Could not load file or assembly 'txtools.dll' or one of its dependencies. The specified module could not be found.

when using the software they get the error 

""Could not load file or assembly 'txtools.dll' or one of its dependencies. The specified module could not be found.""

--Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -

24/06/2026 10:24:34 installing new machine and setting us new printer

--Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -

Run-time error-2147467261 (80004003)': Object reference not set to an instance of an object

Could not load file or assembly 'txtools.dll' or one of its dependencies. The specified module could not be found.

--Look to include screenshots where possible -

--Workaround offered or provided – Yes

--Have you followed all of the steps of the workaround provided on PRB - No

there is no PRB

--Does the current workaround work - No
----If No selected from above state reason why not working and provide screenshots of the errors.

I dont think the customer is doing what i ask them to do and i think this is because they are not giving it to their IT. If they are giving it to IT then their IT dont know what to do.

--What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - 

There are no KBs on this but an old case reference was found.

CS0719727 - which was same issue for another customer

Based on this i have spoken with Dot and checked.

TXTools does exist in c:\smartclient\ascribe\

-----

I advised them of this on 03/07

1. txtools.dll is missing


2. Check the application's installation folder.
Search the PC for txtools.dll.

A dependent DLL is missing

Sometimes txtools.dll exists, but one of the files it depends on does not.
TX Text Control requires several supporting DLLs and the Microsoft Visual C++ runtime. [docs.textcontrol.com]


3. 32-bit / 64-bit mismatch

A 32-bit application trying to load 64-bit DLLs (or vice versa) can produce assembly load errors. [stackoverflow.com]


4. Corrupt or incomplete installation

The software may have been partially removed, updated incorrectly, or antivirus software may have quarantined a DLL. [tutorialpedia.org], [techbloat.com]



Things to try
Option 1:
Repair or reinstall the application
This is usually the fastest fix.

Uninstall the application.
Reboot.
Reinstall using the latest installer.
Launch as Administrator.

Option 2:
Install/repair Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributables
Many DLL loading errors are caused by missing VC++ runtime files. TX Text Control uses Visual C++ runtime components. [docs.textcontrol.com]
Install both:

Microsoft Visual C++ 2015-2022 x64
Microsoft Visual C++ 2015-2022 x86

Option 3:
Check whether txtools.dll exists
Look in the application's program folder.
If it is missing:

Reinstall the application.
Do not download random DLLs from third-party DLL websites.

Option 4:
Check antivirus quarantine
Review:

Windows Security Protection History
Any third-party antivirus quarantine area

Restore the file if it has been quarantined.

--

Their IT apparently checked this and said its not an IT Issue as the printer works.

--

Further investigation was pointing me towards point 2

2. Check the application's installation folder.
Search the PC for txtools.dll.

A dependent DLL is missing

Sometimes txtools.dll exists, but one of the files it depends on does not.
TX Text Control requires several supporting DLLs and the Microsoft Visual C++ runtime.

solution

Option 2:
Install/repair Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributables
Many DLL loading errors are caused by missing VC++ runtime files. TX Text Control uses Visual C++ runtime components. [docs.textcontrol.com]
Install both:

Microsoft Visual C++ 2015-2022 x64
Microsoft Visual C++ 2015-2022 x86

Again this has been checked by their IT -- (i dont think it has)

TXTools.dll does exist in c:\smartclient\ascribe\

After liaising with Andrew Bell he suggested this was because of the missing CTL3D32.dll on windows 11 machines and to do the fix in PRB0052991

I advised the following

--
You advised you have reimaged you laptop and this was also a windows 11 machine.

To fix this can you try the following.

NOTE : This may need to go to your IT to do this.

--Open Powershell (run as admin)

--Copy the following into the powershell screen.

iwr ""https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols/ctl3d32.dll/3005CC7211000/ctl3d32.dll"" -OutFile ""C:\CTL3D32.dll""

--This will put the file CTL3D32.DLL into the route of the C drive. you need to then copy this file into C:\windows\SysWow or C:\windows\SysWow64 depending on your OS

The rerun the emis installer software.

Test the label printing again.

When you machine was upgrade to windows 11 version 25H2. Microsoft removed this DLL which has caused issues relating to DLL files.

--

They have done this and still doesn't work

As per CS0719727 the fix was 

Mo managed to figure out that we needed to reinstall the vcredist_x86.exe package, which fixes the problem. We've run through a couple of PCs to test this and it works, so happy for this call to be closed. I'll liaise with our IT department to make sure this is installed alongside Ascribe or as part of their installation package.

They have reinstalled the software and followed my last instructions as above then this should be working now.

This suggests as per Option 2 fix would work -- Install/repair Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributables

--A clear set of recreation steps -

Just use the software as normal and try to print a label

Could not load file or assembly 'txtools.dll' or one of its dependencies. The specified module could not be found.

