01/07/2026 11:59:45 - Azeem Parvez (Work notes)
I also called stan and also advised the following from Dave Nelson :

there could very well be a performance hit if the VM is using all 8 cores.  The minimum number of vCPUs is governed by how busy the SQL Server is BUT, that said, the minimum number of cores that you can pay for (in licence terms) is 4 so it makes no sense to go lower than 4.
 
Only the customer has visibility of how busy the VM is.  Hopefully they are making that decision based on tangible monitoring evidence and not just cost.

