16/07/2026 12:09:53 - Sean Prescott (Work notes)
Passing to PA's, Minimum data set below :-

A clear description of the Problem -

All application in C:\Ascribe\Smartswitch will not run on the web server

IP 10.102.6.157 - BCHVMASC_P_WB01

Time that the issue was first noticed; was anything specific that user or site (maintenance, upgrade etc) was doing at that point? -

Its been noticed for a long time but no one has ever done anything about it

Details of any error messages appearing and their corresponding error log(s) -

When trying to run the software from the front end an error appears

Saying

You do not have permission to run this file
Inline with policy, we have prevented you from running this file because we believe it may be malicious, putting bupa and its customers at risk.

Program name - Pharmacy Stores
Program Publisher - Ascribe Ltd (Verification Failed)
Program Path - C:\ascribe\smartclient\   (Any EXE in this directory)

If you try to run the program directly from the c:\ascribe\smartclient\ directory same error appears.

Look to include screenshots where possible -

See attached Bupa Cromwell.docx

Workaround offered or provided – No

Have you followed all of the steps of the workaround provided on PRB - No

Does the current workaround work - No
--If No selected from above state reason why not working and provide screenshots of the errors.

What Investigation have you carried out / what knowledge based articles have you used - 

This works when from running the software from the front end client machines

I have been liaising with Emm, Kamini and Grace regarding this

Emm had the same issue back in August when the Test system was being set up

Emm advised she messaged Delroy regarding this to put an exception in on the App Blocker

Bupa IT have rejected this and advised the digital signature on the application itself is not valid

See Cromwell2.docx

After liaising with Kamini and Grace they mentioned they gave Bupa a fix at somepoint because the digital signature didn't have a timestamp.

The screen shots in Cromwell2.docx are from a client machine which doesnt have the timestamp yet it works there. the server is the same but doesn't work

Message from Grace was as follows

Hi Sean, could you raise a PRB for this issue, then we can plan it into the next sprint (21st July) and assign someone to take a look at it

A clear set of recreation steps -

From the web server - IP 10.102.6.157 - BCHVMASC_P_WB01

Open the front end software and open the inpatients - labelling editor

error appears

Open File explorer on the Web server and try to open any application (EXE)

The error will appear.

As mentioned this works on the client machines and software loads up. only slight difference if it means anything is if the end user tries to open the software from File manager they get another error

Stores Module
Unable to connect to database Phase2. - Token not provided

We get the other error, but an end user wouldn't be opening it from the file explorer.

This is causing significant issues when trying to recreate and fault find issue the customer is logging with us and need to be resolved.

